    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0124" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/751: Telxegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-29T04:00:00+01:00">May 29, 1940—4
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Have cabled Kennedy warning against repercussions of steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Roosevelt</hi> charging same price for cots in hold as
                    for cots in public rooms, newspaper correspondents aware of this injustice.
                    Damaging <pb facs="0125" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/> scandal bound to follow,
                    conditions at best bound to create indignation. Steamer announced from America
                    as being sent by Government. No disclaimer will relieve Government of
                    responsibility in public mind. Please show President this telegram if
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
